{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character","id":1415424,"title":"Losing Essence and a 500 Year Old Starting Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-25T09:05:59-07:00","id":1415424,"title":"Losing Essence and a 500 Year Old Starting Character","content":"So I was thinking today about how you can take a Solar or Lunar and lock them up, and rather than endlessly gaining xp like a player character their bodies and minds can just atrophy and they can actually lose charms and dots as they forget things. Then somebody might come along 500 years later to break them out, thinking they\u2019re getting a legendary warlord, and actually getting a shell of what they once were.<br /> <br /> THEN I thought, could that be a PC backstory? Could you lose Essence dots, going all the way from 5 back to 1, after being locked away for half a millennia? Forgetting almost all your charms and any abilities and being left with what you\u2019d get at chargen? Or is Essence something that once you have it can never be lost outside of things like that spiteful sorcery from 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T09:27:37-07:00","id":1415428,"title":"","content":"Atrophy <i>is</i> a thing. PCs don't typically lose dots because that's generally not fun and tracking &quot;How long can I go without using Socialize before my dots start to degrade&quot; is, if anything, <i>less</i> fun, but <i>as a story</i>, that sounds just fine to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T09:40:31-07:00","id":1415430,"title":"","content":"I could see the spiritual refinement that is associated with raising essence being a continuous process. If you spend decades not working on it, you lose it, like an athlete who stops training. But yeah, it shouldn't be a punishment, just a story element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T09:41:44-07:00","id":1415431,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m thinking like during the Shogunate there was a celestial exalt who was just terrorizing certain areas, perhaps over multiple incarnations. Dagn the Destroyer, Terror of Ludcilia, Doom of all Kanobites, etc. Finally they capture him but decide he\u2019s too dangerous to kill so they imprison him in a big secret prison with spirits bound to take care of his needs like water and such. Then jump to present day where the rest of the circle wants to battle the Realm or a Deathlord or something, and they find the location of Dagn\u2019s prison. In session 0 or session 1 they bust open the cell, hoping to find one of the greatest warlords ever, and instead find somebody with weak arms pinned in their magical soul steel shackles, and who barely even remembers how to wield their sword or interact with people after a millennia chained to a wall. THEN they get taken over as a PC and start using experience to re-learn what they\u2019ve forgotten, or maybe even learn a new way. That doesn\u2019t really work if they start as Essence 5 though, their sprit would also have to atrophy or something, but I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s a thing necessarily. Looking at the description on page 174 it seems like it could be, but I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T09:43:33-07:00","id":1415432,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a perfectly cromulent backstory, and who is going to stop you?<br /> <br /> I'd wonder at the character having been Essence 5 at the start of imprisonment, though. Just because such Exalted are so uncommon anyway.<br /> <br /> Mind, it would leave a hanging plot hook of somebody who must have definitely engaged in legendary feats that they can't remember, and looking for the clues to rebuild that identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T10:08:42-07:00","id":1415436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415432#post1415432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like a perfectly cromulent backstory, and who is going to stop you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to keep things consistent. If I had to I could say they used some serious high level essence draining rituals, but that\u2019s not a concept I want to introduce unless it\u2019s necessary<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415432#post1415432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd wonder at the character having been Essence 5 at the start of imprisonment, though. Just because such Exalted are so uncommon anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked 5 because I wanted their legend to be that they terrorized the Shogunate for a long time, something appropriate to E4-E5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415432#post1415432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mind, it would leave a hanging plot hook of somebody who must have definitely engaged in legendary feats that they can't remember, and looking for the clues to rebuild that identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be cool too. Being unable to remember their old identity, and choosing to reject or accept it as they discover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T10:21:29-07:00","id":1415438,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure losing Essence is supported by the base setting fluff. Like Ragara is going senile, but he's not less potent. Debilitation does happen, but reaching higher levels of Enlightenment is the sort of transcendental realization and knowledge that doesn't seem losable, in the base setting. (Without stuff like the Rune of Singular Hatred)<br /> <br /> That being said, as a one-off, or as a result of a terrible decision or deal, or maybe a really nasty Working or something, I could see it happening. I suppose the real question is what you gain from this, that you wouldn't already have from a particularly noteworthy former incarnation? I mean that's half the point of giving Celestials memories of their past lives. Feuds that are and are not your own at the same time. Links to terrible things you did, but don't remember in a former age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T10:40:10-07:00","id":1415440,"title":"","content":"<i>If</i> you have a PC that wants this, then go for it.<br /> <br /> It's in no way setting breaking. Like Misho from Keychain -- It's not canon, but it <i>could be</i> canon.<br /> <br /> It's a cool idea for a backstory.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't hang metaphysics on it.<br /> <br /> It's a cool, unusual PC background. Nothing more. I really wouldn't sell it as &quot;losing Essence&quot;. This is a once mighty PC who has been returned to the level of a starting character for reasons of plot. They're rusty. They're Essence 5... we're just treating them as if they're Essence 1. What is Essence 5 anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-25-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T10:52:06-07:00","id":1415441,"title":"","content":"I don't know that I would necessarily care for this if it were an official part of the setting but as a neat concept intended for a one-off character backstory it seems alright to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T11:14:55-07:00","id":1415443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415438#post1415438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the real question is what you gain from this, that you wouldn't already have from a particularly noteworthy former incarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a couple of things. For one you can\u2019t hide behind being another incarnation. I wasn\u2019t really thinking of the amnesia thing too hard from the outset, just the degradation of skills and body. Like I remember vividly playing Dead Space 3 on Ironman mode but I sure as hell cant do it anymore. I also think it\u2019s a cool start to the story where the rest of the circle thinks they\u2019re getting Queen Merela who\u2019s going to waltz into the Mask of Winter\u2019s palace, put him in a headlock and make him cry without breaking a sweat, and they find someone who\u2019s basically no stronger than any of them already are. As an added bonus you don\u2019t have any attachment to the world right now, your prior life was 1,000 years ago. You get to find meaning in a life that you\u2019d wholly given up on for a dozen mortal lifetimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T12:15:03-07:00","id":1415450,"title":"","content":"Essence ratings aren't diegetic. Essence trait atrophy due to long-term imprisonment is the sort of unusual scenario that isn't expressly covered by the rules, and insofar as PC traits don't diminish, that's for protection against Storyteller shenanigans rather than setting physics. This seems perfectly reasonable to me, barring any strong negative reaction from fellow players at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T13:23:27-07:00","id":1415454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415443#post1415443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well a couple of things. For one you can\u2019t hide behind being another incarnation. I wasn\u2019t really thinking of the amnesia thing too hard from the outset, just the degradation of skills and body. Like I remember vividly playing Dead Space 3 on Ironman mode but I sure as hell cant do it anymore. I also think it\u2019s a cool start to the story where the rest of the circle thinks they\u2019re getting Queen Merela who\u2019s going to waltz into the Mask of Winter\u2019s palace, put him in a headlock and make him cry without breaking a sweat, and they find someone who\u2019s basically no stronger than any of them already are. As an added bonus you don\u2019t have any attachment to the world right now, your prior life was 1,000 years ago. You get to find meaning in a life that you\u2019d wholly given up on for a dozen mortal lifetimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But (assuming you're skipping the Amnesia bit), absolutely none of that requires anything more than Essence 2 to start with. I mean Queen Merala, sure might not be doable. But especially in 3E, one can be a legendary unstoppable warrior with pretty much just the Supernal. Then add a few thousand years of misinformation, propaganda, and outright lies, and it's absolutely possible that Eyes of Iron, the legendary Invulnerable Sword Princess, defeater of directional wargods, Slayer of Shogunate Legions, is a Solar who really is an (optimized) starting character.<br /> <br /> The genre (drawing from everything from Star Wars to Kill Bill to Kung-Fu Hustle) is that the ancient master who lives in isolation is likely to be far /more/ in tune with the deeper secrets of the Art than normal people. Maybe rusty, less skill. But if I told you there was an ancient master on a hidden mountaintop, who hadn't left the mountain for a hundred years, the general assumption is that he's a wise and potent dude, with a better grasp of the Truths of Reality than someone else. Now obviously, Exalted has its own vibe, and is not actually just kung-fu movie-based. But they used many of the same tropes and thematic beats, which is why people who go raise their essence often, if not always, go into isolation to do so. It just seems very counter to the themes of Exalted, and the way the setting ties Essence to experience (and Experience) and (much looser in 3E, but still somewhat) to age.<br /> <br /> That being said, I totally support a character who remembers the ancient past because he lived it. Things like the Veil That Holds Back Time are built to let you tell these kinds of stories, IMO. I've seen a really interesting character built in previous editions who was Veiled into the future during the Usurpation (and had Savant) but they were a rookie solar, and hence a regular PC (except for background access). Especially if the Veil (or the working, or whatever) is broken when you wake up, it wouldn't even cost you anything. Or one who was sorta like Misho. (I had a PC with amnesia before her Exaltation, throwback and a lot of past life memories in a game I ran).<br /> <br /> TL;DR - I agree with the above posters. So long as everybody at the table is cool with it (particularly your ST and any Lore characters), have fun. But as a fundamental setting thing, I find losing Essence because you're old and isolated to be unthematic and counter to the canon examples (such as they are) of characters who are obviously faded glories, with diminished capacities, but who still have essence scores commensurate with their achievements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-25-2020, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T15:17:28-07:00","id":1415466,"title":"","content":"I'm of the same mind as Scrollreader: I would find your execution of this incongruous with my own understanding of the setting conceits, but I'm not at your table. <br /> <br /> That said, I think the core idea, of a legendary hero brought down to the power levels of their early days, is a great idea and if you were at my table I'd definitely want to find a way to work with you on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T16:23:03-07:00","id":1415472,"title":"","content":"You could also have a character who say, was a super powerful Exalt in their day, but were betrayed by their rivals and cursed and injured and lessened in some fashion, rather than having their skills straight atrophy. Greatest swordsman in the world without their sword-arm, and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T16:50:17-07:00","id":1415477,"title":"","content":"The image I've been getting is of... basically Gollum, come to think of it. Confined in a cramped and dark space with nothing to do but brood in solitude and live off of whatever crawling or swimming things you can snatch up.<br /> <br /> At least your anima banner can provide you with light, but is that much comfort if it just illuminates the same few walls every day? You might have an innate sense of the passage of time, but I feel if we expand beyond game mechanics it would make sense to feel quite dissociated from that after long enough with no frames of reference or direct exposure. It all starts blending together.<br /> <br /> After all, the proposition is centuries of this. Assuming a character who didn't go in strongly for mental discipline to tolerate asceticism, that could mess somebody up even without it being a supernaturally empowered place like the Tombs of Atuan or something.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm thinking an Eclipse Caste for this. Not just from thinking that's the most likely spread of deeply invested Abilities to not afford ready means of escape, but there's a strong juxtaposition between a character that might have been all about traveling widely and freely and engaging with a variety of other people and a fate of being confined alone for generations.<br /> <br /> You're like Aang! But conscious the whole time, which is five times longer, and with no big cuddly companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T17:02:42-07:00","id":1415478,"title":"","content":"This sounds cool, its easy to work into setting fluff, and its not like it breaks any mechanics. If they are E5 then they basically have to predate the Usurpation and emerge in the present by some means, and that should tie in to how weakened they are. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Jasper Blue-Star</b> was a legendary explorer of the First Age, being born after the Great Primoridal War he lusted for the glories and sights of his mentors. He sailed far out into the Wyld, he sailed to Yu Shan, to the bottom of the sea, and to the dreamless void that lies beyond the beyond. On his way home from such an adventure, he was betrayed by his entire crew- Dragonblood sailors and soldiers who had been kept abreast of the plans for Usurpation by cunning sorcery. Falling into the murky mixwater where the Dreaming Sea meets the Wyld, he was cast around by rough seas of magic for both incalculable ages and the briefest of moments. Who can say how the ravaging of time works in the flowing seas of unreality? Severely weakened by the ordeal, he washes up on shore in the Age of Sorrows, his divine flame weakened but not extinguished. He sets off across the land, hungry for information and desperate for allies. His greatest journey lies ahead of him still...</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T17:22:59-07:00","id":1415481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415477#post1415477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The image I've been getting is of... basically Gollum, come to think of it. <br /> <br /> You're like Aang! But conscious the whole time, which is five times longer, and with no big cuddly companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, Oldboy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T18:45:17-07:00","id":1415493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415454#post1415454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. But (assuming you're skipping the Amnesia bit), absolutely none of that requires anything more than Essence 2 to start with. I mean Queen Merala, sure might not be doable. But especially in 3E, one can be a legendary unstoppable warrior with pretty much just the Supernal. Then add a few thousand years of misinformation, propaganda, and outright lies, and it's absolutely possible that Eyes of Iron, the legendary Invulnerable Sword Princess, defeater of directional wargods, Slayer of Shogunate Legions, is a Solar who really is an (optimized) starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a VERY optimized one that I mostly classify as abusing mechanics rather than intended design. Yeah, you can technically make a character with a defining intimacy for &quot;Whenever I'm fighting&quot; and tie that to that to Divine Executioner Stance and yatta yatta, but I don't really think that represents what an Essence 1 Solar is supposed to feel like. Keeping in mind here that the Shogunate was dealing with Essence 6-7 Lunars with powerful artifacts like the Book of Three Circles that lets a Lunar cast Solar Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Either way, that kind of character very well could make the Mask of Winters cry like a baby, so the whole unlocking the prison to unveil the great hero of old who can save everyone actually does just unlock the great hero of old who can save everyone.<br /> <br /> There's no sens that there was the great person that you were, legendary even among the Exalted, and now have been brought low again through the ravages of lonely eons. Now free, though, to build yourself again, to remake what you once were, or something new entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415454#post1415454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The genre (drawing from everything from Star Wars to Kill Bill to Kung-Fu Hustle) is that the ancient master who lives in isolation is likely to be far /more/ in tune with the deeper secrets of the Art than normal people. Maybe rusty, less skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but this isn't self isolation on a mountaintop where you can commune with the world and endlessly perfect katas, it's isolation somewhere specifically devoid of essence and likely with restraints that prevent free movement of any kind. Experience points are a player character game thing anyway, not an in universe thing. Player characters can end up with enough xp to gain Essence 5 in less than a year, and that's definitely not something any NPC gets.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking like an intro fiction something like this...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There are dark places of the world, the deep crevasses that even the gods do not know. They do not know because they were never meant to be. When the Titans first molded the earth and the seas and pressed them together, these were the forgotten places. These were the little folds between places that formed then. It is in one of the deepest, darkest of these folds that three figures now labor under the light of three flickering lanterns.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you certain this is the door?&quot; said one hunched over the sixteenth, and final lock.<br /> <br /> The tall one standing up replied flatly &quot;Are you kidding? This location was from the third-hand account of somebody who said they read the journal of the architect.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first replied without looking up &quot;Okay, so that's not giving me a lot of confidence that I'm not about to unleash a horrible demon.&quot;<br /> <br /> The scholar nodded, seeming to be undisturbed. &quot;I am 100% sure that the builders of this place thought it was a demon, and 70% sure it is the one we seek.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thief's breath caught in her throat as, unexpectedly soon, the lock hitched and turned, sliding open. For a few seconds that seemed to last an eternity all was still in this place of forgotten dark, even the lanterns grew still, and dim. Then when no great horror burst forth, the third figure stood and reached forward, grasping the enormous jade handles and pulling hard the doors swung open. Even in this there was an eerie stillness, a whisper of nothing more than dust as the great mass split apart to reveal the sole captive of this prison.<br /> <br /> It was a figure sat cross-legged on the floor with their head bowed, cord-thin chains of soulsteel fastened to shackles on their neck, wrists and ankles. Everywhere, on the floor, the doors, and even covering the figure themselves, was a thick layer of dust. Some of this now trickled off the head of the captive as they turned their head away. Eyes that have seen nought but perfect darkness, and ears that have heard nought but perfect silence for centuries now bombarded with light and sound.<br /> <br /> The trio stood there, stunned. The prisoner then looked up at them with thin, watery eyes, and placed a slim hand on the floor in front of them. Shakily, they clambered into a standing position, the chains making a quiet hiss as they slid across the dust on the ground. Each movement creaked bone and cracked joints that have sat still for decades at least. Having not spoken to another soul for so long, dragging thoughts into speech was like walking through molasses. The words came out slow and awkward, but deliberate.<br /> <br /> &quot;How long?&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-25-2020, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T19:49:15-07:00","id":1415497,"title":"","content":"The real potential issue of this is that somebody who didn't have a at least moderate amount of integrity charms would have gone completely insane far before even his first 100 years of complete isolation.<br /> <br /> The second issue is that, the first point isn't even talking about the potential of the Great Curse to do the same. Especially since being trapped for centuries means they'd likely be confronted that the things they care about most are now out of their reach to effect or preserve.<br /> <br /> But again if your table thinks it's cool, then more story to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","user":"Chronos12","date":". 09-25-2020, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T19:50:26-07:00","id":1415498,"title":"","content":"Right. But the unjustly imprisoned guy (Oldboy or The Bride or The Count of Monte Cristo or the Man in the Iron Mask or The Beast from Kung Fu Hustle) is basically just a montage and a shave away from kicking ass in their chosen field. I'm having trouble coming up with someone (besides an Elder Evil/Sauron sort of thing) that demonstrates what you are looking for. Gollum doesn't lose power from his cave living, but from losing the Ring, which is actually what has the Power. Do you have a literary or movie example? In most of the examples I can think of, they either come back with Incredible Motivation as basically a Randian Superpower, or having basically not lost a step, or only minimally so, before they suddenly regain their secret Technique. Very rarely is imprisonment, particularly of a hero, actually emasculating. (Maiming is a little more common). And it's particularly rare to lose a secret Technique, or ancient wisdom. If anything, they usually gain from their experience, in either wisdom or motivation.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm really not trying to Bah Humbug your stuff. I adore that intro. It's great for that flavor. But even if physically crippled, and unable to perform the Secret Technique (unlikely for the Exalted) that's the sort of Wizened Master who has the knowledge and the power to teach it to the young hero. And generally, that sort of wisdom and mastery is represented in Exalted by higher essence, and the charms it unlocks. I have zero problem with the PCs unearthing an ancient crippled Exalt. That's awesome. I'm just having difficulty seeing how that's supposed to damage his transcendental understanding of Creation. Stymie further development? Sure. And maybe while he was trapped they stole his power with evil sorcery? Fantastic. I just don't think the setting represents it being something that can be lost because you ... were trapped . You don't lose essence when you abandon the strictures of the Immaculate Coils. You don't lose essence when you completely restructure your belief system. You don't lose essence when you alter your world-view for Sorcery or Necromancy. And the older NPCs we see, even ones who are stated to be declining? Don't have low essence scores.<br /> <br /> Even the meanest of the Exalted is capable of overcoming the ancient and unkillable enemies of the gods. I don't see imprisonment, even in the heart of Malfeas as being enough to forget that. They can be killed. They can choose to surrender to corruption. They can be defeated or crippled. And they can be the victim of greater powers, sorcery and shaping. But I don't think they can be bored or bound to lesser their mastery of their self and Creation. But that's my take on the feel and the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-25-2020, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T20:28:01-07:00","id":1415500,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to go even further than Scrollreader and say that, in my mind, if you\u2019re Exalted and something as trivial as \u201cCan\u2019t move\u201d stops you from going full Uncle Iroh it\u2019s because you weren\u2019t as motivated as he was. 500 years is plenty of time to figure out how to work out through muscle tensing alone, truly oppose yourself in hyper-detailed mental exercises, etc., not to mention if you don\u2019t come out with a dozen Essence 5 meditation Charms then what even <i>were</i> you doing all that time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T21:55:29-07:00","id":1415504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415431#post1415431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I\u2019m thinking like during the Shogunate there was a celestial exalt who was just terrorizing certain areas, perhaps over multiple incarnations. Dagn the Destroyer, Terror of Ludcilia, Doom of all Kanobites, etc. Finally they capture him but decide he\u2019s too dangerous to kill so they imprison him in a big secret prison with spirits bound to take care of his needs like water and such. Then jump to present day where the rest of the circle wants to battle the Realm or a Deathlord or something, and they find the location of Dagn\u2019s prison. In session 0 or session 1 they bust open the cell, hoping to find one of the greatest warlords ever, and instead find somebody with weak arms pinned in their magical soul steel shackles, and who barely even remembers how to wield their sword or interact with people after a millennia chained to a wall. THEN they get taken over as a PC and start using experience to re-learn what they\u2019ve forgotten, or maybe even learn a new way. That doesn\u2019t really work if they start as Essence 5 though, their sprit would also have to atrophy or something, but I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s a thing necessarily. Looking at the description on page 174 it seems like it could be, but I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, i think Essence 3-4 could be respectable enough, with Celestial Circle Sorcery, a good Supernal and a decent spread of Ess 1-3 solar charms (or artifact evocations) such a person would already be head and shoulders above a pretty large chunk of the exalts in its past era, as most Celestial exalts would be below that and among those Sidereals and Lunars that did have Ess3+, not every one will have Sorcery or other gimmicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T22:08:42-07:00","id":1415506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415498#post1415498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But the unjustly imprisoned guy (Oldboy or The Bride or The Count of Monte Cristo or the Man in the Iron Mask or The Beast from Kung Fu Hustle) is basically just a montage and a shave away from kicking ass in their chosen field. I'm having trouble coming up with someone (besides an Elder Evil/Sauron sort of thing) that demonstrates what you are looking for. Gollum doesn't lose power from his cave living, but from losing the Ring, which is actually what has the Power. Do you have a literary or movie example?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a trope that I'm thinking of. There was just a developer who commented a while ago that imprisoned exalts do not just continue to improve in abilities and may* even lose dots. Which makes sense, it's not a narrative trope necessarily, but Exalted are the dragons from the Discworld, they don't run on Narrativium. Their skills may deteriorate and their muscles may atrophy because that's just what happens when you don't use skills or get exercise.<br /> <br /> *MAY here, not definitely-always-do-no-you-can't-have-a-badass-prison-montage just that they don't keep gaining xp and will eventually get out because they effectively have access to their own character sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415500#post1415500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m going to go even further than Scrollreader and say that, in my mind, if you\u2019re Exalted and something as trivial as \u201cCan\u2019t move\u201d stops you from going full Uncle Iroh it\u2019s because you weren\u2019t as motivated as he was. 500 years is plenty of time to figure out how to work out through muscle tensing alone, truly oppose yourself in hyper-detailed mental exercises, etc., not to mention if you don\u2019t come out with a dozen Essence 5 meditation Charms then what even <i>were</i> you doing all that time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at Sesus Nagezzer, he was a rising star in the Imperial legions, a hero, and his &quot;promising destiny died abruptly the day that his pursuit of the dangerous spirit Wind Across the Savanna ended in his maiming.&quot; How come he didn't just exalt up and get his leg fixed? Surely getting a crippled leg back in working order is easier than building up the skills to escape an artifact N/A prison while your essence is constantly being drained?<br /> <br /> Maybe the character in question just isn't as motivated as Iroh. They don't have that kind of iron will, or maybe they just can't force their body to do the things some other Solars can.<br /> <br /> Here, look at it like this. In real life I could theoretically have a human character sheet, and theoretically so could Usain Bolt. If you looked at both our character sheets you might go &quot;Hey, you're both humans, if you wanted to you could just spend some xp and get roughly the 9.6 seconds for the 100m dash&quot; That's not actually how it works though, that's just exploiting a necessary simplification to represent real life as a kind of RPG.<br /> <br /> Maybe the prison break requires Nine Aeon's Thews, and theoretically some Solar could do that, sure, but not the one who's in there now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-26-2020, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T23:52:36-07:00","id":1415510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415498#post1415498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gollum doesn't lose power from his cave living, but from losing the Ring, which is actually what has the Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but living in the cave made him less pretty and talking in rambling circles to himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a literary or movie example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, but nor do I require one to imagine physical and mental atrophy after a long period of strenuous and unengaging confinement.<br /> <br /> I suppose my example is based mostly on accounts of what it's like to experience solitary confinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T07:59:02-07:00","id":1415538,"title":"","content":"Fundamentally, I think maybe we disagree on what permanent essence is supposed to represent. While the book describes it as both power and enlightenment, I lean towards the latter, particularly in a metaphysical or setting sense (though I am aware the character doesn't know his number, there is a sense that some people are more in tune with their essence, or capable of deeper and more significant effects). If you see permanent essence as a muscle, then you can see it atrophying. But if it is Enlightenment, a new way of realizing the truths of the world, then you can never really lose that, without attacks on your very soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-26-2020, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:33:53-07:00","id":1415544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415538#post1415538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if it is Enlightenment, a new way of realizing the truths of the world, then you can never really lose that, without attacks on your very soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno so much about that; even setting aside a person's capacity to forget, overwrite, or otherwise lose sight of something they once learned, there's a non-zero number of schools of thought (be they religions, philosophies, whatever), where you have cosmic wisdom or whatever, and the world can take it from you, or at least cause you to lose your grasp on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo me it all kinda goes back to the question of, &quot;Are the Exalted human?&quot; Plateauing is human. Finding your skills have gone rusty with disuse is human. Losing your grip on reality from protracted periods of isolation is <i>all too</i> human, so <b>I</b> won't <i>categorically </i>rule it out, because I like my Exalted to be human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:38:48-07:00","id":1415548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415544#post1415544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bTo me it all kinda goes back to the question of, &quot;Are the Exalted human?&quot; Plateauing is human. Finding your skills have gone rusty with disuse is human. Losing your grip on reality from protracted periods of isolation is <i>all too</i> human, so <b>I</b> won't <i>categorically </i>rule it out, because I like my Exalted to be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I view the Exalted as something more than human. And also fully human. Not to drag too much real world religion into things, but similar to how many versions of Christianity view Jesus as being both fully human AND fully divine. The Shard, the Divine Essence is perfected and sublime. The person, the host is fully mortal and fallible. An Exalt is both. But especially in 3E, where there are no mortals with command of their essence, that part of it is more of the divine and perfected portion, in my view of the setting.<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, I do think an Exalt could go crazy from isolation, or lose muscle or have skills go rusty from disuse (though I'd totally allow a PC to Uncle Iroh stunt their way past that, and potentially even use imprisonment as training time). I think they're generally more resilient to such things than mortals, but that works for me. But I view an increased permanent essence as more transcendental, and probably immune to such vagaries, because command of essence is Not mortal. I think it takes a potent spiritual attack directly on that to damage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-26-2020, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:37:11-07:00","id":1415561,"title":"","content":"Essence isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> Mnemon isn't sitting there thinking &quot;I meditated on the Earth four times... so that means I'm Essence 5.&quot;<br /> <br /> The trait is an abstraction of your capabilities. If your capabilities decrease, your trait descreases.<br /> <br /> You don't become less enlightened by losing dots of Essence.<br /> When you close your eye to the world, turn aside from the truths you once learned to embrace darkness and despair, and forget the face of your father, then you lose dots of Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:46:40-07:00","id":1415565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415498#post1415498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But the unjustly imprisoned guy (Oldboy or The Bride or The Count of Monte Cristo or the Man in the Iron Mask or The Beast from Kung Fu Hustle) is basically just a montage and a shave away from kicking ass in their chosen field. I'm having trouble coming up with someone (besides an Elder Evil/Sauron sort of thing) that demonstrates what you are looking for. Gollum doesn't lose power from his cave living, but from losing the Ring, which is actually what has the Power. Do you have a literary or movie example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Man in Black/Dread Pirate Weasley<br /> Darth Vader<br /> Gollum<br /> Reek/Theion Greyjoy<br /> Apollo Creed (after Rocky kicks his ass)<br /> Druss the Legend (kinda, in the first book)<br /> Voldemort (yes, Elder Evil sort of thing -- but Tonks also shows this a little, and the Longbottoms, whilst Sirus Black is somewhere between atrophy and awesome)<br /> King Piccalo, Majin Buu, Frieza<br /> Professor X (days of future past version)<br /> Thor, Captain Marvel, World Breaker Hulk, Post-Crisis Wally<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In most of the examples I can think of, they either come back with Incredible Motivation as basically a Randian Superpower, or having basically not lost a step, or only minimally so, before they suddenly regain their secret Technique. </div> </div> </div>That's this trope. Right here.<br /> <br /> As an NPC, your Solar took a thousand years to reach Essence 5. You reach Essence 5 again as a PC within, like, six months. Like Inago Montoya or Locke Lamora.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-26-2020, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:47:25-07:00","id":1415566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415561#post1415561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't become less enlightened by losing dots of Essence.<br /> When you close your eye to the world, turn aside from the truths you once learned to embrace darkness and despair, and forget the face of your father, then you lose dots of Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the absurd puissance of the First Age Solars implies that this isn't the default assumption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T10:30:29-07:00","id":1415570,"title":"","content":"Importantly, however--how important is it to quantify that &quot;I was at Essence 5 and now I'm at Essence 1&quot;? Especially given that in your Supernal that doesn't mean anything for your charm selections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T11:47:16-07:00","id":1415579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415538#post1415538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if it is Enlightenment, a new way of realizing the truths of the world, then you can never really lose that, without attacks on your very soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that being put in such a state may constitute an attack on your soul, especially for somebody who defined their life by their freedom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415570#post1415570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Importantly, however--how important is it to quantify that &quot;I was at Essence 5 and now I'm at Essence 1&quot;? Especially given that in your Supernal that doesn't mean anything for your charm selections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 5 might not be required, but more than 1 I think is. The backstory for the character in question was that they were a notably powerful exalt in their time. Among exalts like Raksi, Chejop Kejak, the Scarlett Empress, etc, they were counted as being likewise dangerous. Supernal is a pretty powerful thing, but it's not Essence 7, not to mention it could be a Lunar anyway who doesn't have Supernal.<br /> <br /> The other part of this is that they lost whatever they once were. Whatever they were, the greatest sorcerer in the world, divine sea captain, invincible warrior, they aren't that anymore. They're not nothing anymore, they're still a Solar or a Lunar, but when you think you're getting Chejop Kejak and you're actually getting a chargen Sidereal with a wide spread of abilities that's a big step down.<br /> <br /> You could have it without the Essence drop and just loss of abilities/attributes and forgetting charms, but they'd still have the motepool and (Essence) calculations, and the ability to start taking Essence 4 charms right away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T13:49:53-07:00","id":1415592,"title":"","content":"We can agree to disagree on the question of permanent Essence loss, I think. I don't think either of us will convince the other. That aside, I do have another issue to bring up.<br /> <br /> Although I don't think it's your intention, I would absolutely be worried about someone coming to the table with this character as a PC or GMNPC. &quot;Yes, I've been reduced to the state of you other PCs. Yes, you're the most legendary swordsman of your age, but I knew many more skilled. I was too powerful for the Elder Sidereals to destroy.&quot; Again, I don't believe this is your intention. But I would definitely make sure everyone at the table is explicitly consenting to the concept, just as if one PC wants to start with Lilith or Leviathan as his Lunar mate. Either you're disappointing the character, because NPCs don't react to his (historical) potency as they should, or you're bending the entire game arc around him, if they do. Games where the plot arc is particularly focused on one PC can definitely work, but it invokes the Dark Fate/Enemy/Dying flaw problem from previous editions, where either the entire game becomes about solving the problems of character X.<br /> <br /> That being said, there's no game police, and if you and everyone at your table is having fun, you probably shouldn't worry about my personal views on the metaphysics of Exalted. I'm always happy to give my opinions here when asked, but ultimately, if it makes sense to you and is fun for your group, Great. It certainly sounds like you have a firm idea in your head of how you want this character to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T04:31:44-07:00","id":1415669,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly wondering what this complicated backstory achieves that simply having vivid past life memories doesn't.<br /> <br /> &quot;My character recalls being super powerful, but now they aren't&quot;<br /> <br /> That's like, every solar in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T04:37:23-07:00","id":1415671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415669#post1415669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly wondering what this complicated backstory achieves that simply having vivid past life memories doesn't.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;My character recalls being super powerful, but now they aren't&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That's like, every solar in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Chapter Fiction in Fangs At the Gate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T04:48:46-07:00","id":1415672,"title":"","content":"The silent pearl stuff? Yeah, ok, there's plot to be had there, but aren't they supposed to be just as powerful as they used to be? <br /> <br /> A first age solar reduced to newbie levels still just feels like reincarnation with extra steps. A lot of spirits will treat a reincarnated exalt as their past self anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T04:59:15-07:00","id":1415674,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26421_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26421\" data-vbnamecard=\"26421\">Scrollreader</a>, I think this is a good point; is &quot;Essence&quot; as a trait fundamentally more like a knowledge, either conscious or intuitive, that exists in a character mind about how to use and perceive essence, or is it more like an awakening of a deeper union between a persons and their Exaltation which is independent of their mind and knowledge and can't really be lost simply by forgetting? The game setting doesn't really say, so it's up to us to decide which feels more right.<br /> <br /> I think such a character like DrLoveMonkey describes would work even if the lost all their Abilities, Attributes and Charms, which are reliant on their knowledge and experience, but retained their Essence score, tho. (Under the &quot;Essence Imperishable&quot; assumption).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T05:28:10-07:00","id":1415675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415674#post1415674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I think this is a good point; is &amp;quot;Essence&amp;quot; as a trait fundamentally more like a knowledge, either conscious or intuitive, that exists in a character mind about how to use and perceive essence, or is it more like an awakening of a deeper union between a persons and their Exaltation which is independent of their mind and knowledge and can't really be lost simply by forgetting? The game setting doesn't really say, so it's up to us to decide which feels more right.<br /> <br /> I think such a character like DrLoveMonkey describes would work even if the lost all their Abilities, Attributes and Charms, which are reliant on their knowledge and experience, but retained their Essence score, tho. (Under the &amp;quot;Essence Imperishable&amp;quot; assumption).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think either approach works. And I think just having one PC (not a DM PC) just start play as a superbadass (Misho style) also works.<br /> <br /> But from a game balance PoV, having all the characters built with the same rules at the same &quot;starting character&quot; level makes sense. If a PC came to me with an interesting back ground that didn't totally wreck the game, I'd roll with it.<br /> <br /> I really don't think &quot;my character lost Essence&quot; is any more derailing than &quot;my character was a mortal Dynast&quot; or &quot;I am the Mask of Winter's reincarnation&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's not going to fit every group or every game. But I'd rather all my PCs start on a (roughly) even keel.<br /> <br /> Like how Assassin's Creed starts with basically all the abilities unlocked then you lose them all. (And most Metroid games now I think on it.) You can have a great &quot;the Essence was inside you all along!&quot; moment as mental blocks are lifted or whatever.<br /> <br /> I really don't think it's useful to use game mechanics to deep dive into metaphysics. Even if a character <i>can't</i> lose Essence, I'd treat them rules-wise as if they were Essence 1 as a pure gameplay mechanic. An abstraction justifying cool fluff.<br /> <br /> Unless you're Netchurching Vitae Efficiency Units, I really don't see how you'd ever know someone's Essence score in play anyway.<br /> <br /> &quot;This character used to be more powerful but has atrophied in prison.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T05:49:36-07:00","id":1415677,"title":"","content":"This is true; there's not, at root, really a difference in game terms between having a Flaw marked on a char sheet where a character has limited control of their 'true' Essence due to imprisonment and atrophy and so cannot access Charms, etc., and just setting Essence at a lower score. I do think it's OK and interesting to explore the ideas behind what advancing in Essence really means, as long as you suggest, we are not too much letting mechanical abstractions dictate and drive that conversation, or even overrule that conversation where it conflicts with underlying setting information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T07:44:30-07:00","id":1415682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415498#post1415498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a literary or movie example?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was imprisoned by his allies, not his enemies, but Link comes out of the Shrine of Resurrection in <i>Breath of the Wild</i> in a <i>vastly</i> reduced state, if the cutscenes from his recovered memories indicate anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T08:31:31-07:00","id":1415686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415682#post1415682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was imprisoned by his allies, not his enemies, but Link comes out of the Shrine of Resurrection in <i>Breath of the Wild</i> in a <i>vastly</i> reduced state, if the cutscenes from his recovered memories indicate anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right. On the other hand, the narrative beat of &quot;sealed away to recover from mortal wounds&quot; resonates a little differently than &quot;locked away because he could not be killed&quot;, and the former resonates more to me with emerging in a greatly weakened state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T08:36:29-07:00","id":1415687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415675#post1415675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think it's useful to use game mechanics to deep dive into metaphysics. Even if a character <i>can't</i> lose Essence, I'd treat them rules-wise as if they were Essence 1 as a pure gameplay mechanic. An abstraction justifying cool fluff.<br /> <br /> Unless you're Netchurching Vitae Efficiency Units, I really don't see how you'd ever know someone's Essence score in play anyway.<br /> <br /> &quot;This character used to be more powerful but has atrophied in prison.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And tbh that was what I was getting at by asking about &quot;how important is it for this character to have Essence 5 in their background&quot;. I am fine with your summary, but the devil is in the details. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T11:04:30-07:00","id":1415701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415592#post1415592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I don't think it's your intention, I would absolutely be worried about someone coming to the table with this character as a PC or GMNPC. &quot;Yes, I've been reduced to the state of you other PCs. Yes, you're the most legendary swordsman of your age, but I knew many more skilled. I was too powerful for the Elder Sidereals to destroy.&quot; Again, I don't believe this is your intention. But I would definitely make sure everyone at the table is explicitly consenting to the concept, just as if one PC wants to start with Lilith or Leviathan as his Lunar mate. Either you're disappointing the character, because NPCs don't react to his (historical) potency as they should, or you're bending the entire game arc around him, if they do. Games where the plot arc is particularly focused on one PC can definitely work, but it invokes the Dark Fate/Enemy/Dying flaw problem from previous editions, where either the entire game becomes about solving the problems of character X.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, and the thing is after the initial disappointment the story doesn't necessarily revolve around The Destroyer. Once the rest of the party realizes he can't just activate Ascendant Battle Visage and Nine Aeon's Thews and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DPuVTPcus-4\" target=\"_blank\">air juggle</a> the Juggernaut, then the plot moves on. The one PC <i>was </i>going to be the easy solution that solves everyone's problems, and now isn't, so what the crap do we all do now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415669#post1415669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly wondering what this complicated backstory achieves that simply having vivid past life memories doesn't.<br /> <br /> &quot;My character recalls being super powerful, but now they aren't&quot;<br /> <br /> That's like, every solar in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's a bit different, in that there was no other life before the exaltation. It's not a farmboy who grew up with a family and at the age of 30 exalts and suddenly has a bunch of memories from a life that wasn't theirs. Rather than the pre-story being that they were a weak mortal who inherited an unimaginable potential for power, they were a capital G God of their time, who became broken and now has to find a way to mend themselves after being given the gift of freedom by their fellow PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T11:16:01-07:00","id":1415705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415682#post1415682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was imprisoned by his allies, not his enemies, but Link comes out of the Shrine of Resurrection in <i>Breath of the Wild</i> in a <i>vastly</i> reduced state, if the cutscenes from his recovered memories indicate anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Disney adaptation of Maui? Imprisoned for a long time, stripped of his artifact hook, he gets the hook back thinking that's all he needed, but still no dice, he has to relearn everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T15:14:15-07:00","id":1415744,"title":"","content":"Ben Gunn in Treasure Island is also possibly another, less fantastical, example for Scrollreader. He's permanently diminished having been trapped on the island, but he's still useful/capable and gets better (ish).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T17:22:18-07:00","id":1415761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415424-losing-essence-and-a-500-year-old-starting-character?p=1415686#post1415686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're right. On the other hand, the narrative beat of &amp;quot;sealed away to recover from mortal wounds&amp;quot; resonates a little differently than &amp;quot;locked away because he could not be killed&amp;quot;, and the former resonates more to me with emerging in a greatly weakened state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prisoners being permitted to exercise is a fairly recent phenomenon, and even then not applied evenly across the world.<br /> <br /> Did you ever watch Firefly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}